// xfail: E268
// test_e268_unknown_stmt_annotation.bpp — an unknown statement-level
// annotation must be REJECTED, never silently swallowed. Until the
// 2026-07-07 faxina the parser ate any `@word` before a statement as a
// vestigial "dispatch hint" nothing ever read (classify_loop compared the
// stored packed token against 1/2/3 — no match possible), so `@par` — or a
// typo like `@profle` — vanished without a trace and the program compiled
// as if nothing had been written. The only statement-level annotation is
// `@profile("zone")`; loop dispatch is automatic (and `@safe` lives on the
// function signature, not here).
main() {
    auto i, s;
    i = 0;
    s = 0;
    @par while (i < 10) {
        s = s + i;
        i = i + 1;
    }
    return s;
}
